 who  bravely rushed in to save his friend  from a villain  and kirishima knows that this kid was  deku kirishima says that being a hero  has nothing to do with being strong or  being  special it's all about that type of  heroic attitude which drove a young  deku to risk his own life to save his  friend  after kirishima says this the rest of  class 1a converges on the spot where he  deku anida are standing mina also calls  out to deku  and asks him to come back to them so  that they can all return to ua  together but deku is still being  stubborn  he says that he would love to go back  but it's just too dangerous  there are too many people seeking  shelter at the ua right now  and he doesn't want to make them a  target for the villains  that is when bakugou himself steps in  bakugo says that back when they were  kids he had always looked down on deku  because  deku was quirkless in some ways deku was  way behind  bakugo mainly in terms of strength and  power since bakugo had a great  flashy quirk and deku had nothing but  in other ways bakugou actually felt that  deku was  always far ahead of him i assume that  bakugo is referring to deku's kindness  and compassion  and his courage and strength of  character even in the face of being  quirkless  it was easy for bakugo to be popular  confident and brave when he was born  with an incredibly strong  quirk but the fact that deku had such  inner courage  strength and resolve despite being born  quirkless  was something that bakugou couldn't  relate to and so bakugou was clearly  self-conscious  about this fact bakugou didn't want to  admit to himself that deep down he  actually felt inferior to deku  and so he compensated by belittling deku  and putting him down  bakugo knows that the way he treated  deku had nothing to do with  deku himself bakugo acted that way  because he himself was insecure  and he couldn't stand the fact that a  quirkless kid was in some ways  superior to him bakugou then proceeds to  finally fully apologize to deku for  everything that he had done to him  in the past bakugou proclaims that deku  has been faithful to the ideals of  all might and that he acted like a true  hero up to this point  as we know this is extremely high praise  from someone like bakugo since bakugo  also deeply respects and idolizes all  might  it's also funny to see bakugo  apologizing like this when in the anime  he's still being a jerk most of the time  but this moment has been a long time  coming so i'm very happy that this  finally happened bakugou really did  mistreat deku for many years  and although he has definitely developed  a lot since then  this public apology to deku is the  culmination of bakugo's progression from  an insecure bully to a true hero  and a true friend after apologizing to  deku in front of everyone  bakugo goes on to say that deku's heroic  ideals can only take him  so far he has reached his limit he can  barely stand  on his own and now is the time for deku  to  trust his friends sure all might like to  do everything on his own  and that is what deku has been doing up  to this point but in order to actually  surpass  all might deku has to accept that the  most effective way to protect the ua  from the villains is for everyone to  work together  and this is such an interesting moment  since deku finally realizes that he is  ahead of his classmates in terms of  physical strength  but they are ahead of him in terms of  emotional strength  and so as he collapses to the ground  deku apologizes to his classmates for  saying that they can't keep up with him  bakugou then grabs deku before deku hits  the ground  and all of class 1a is clearly affected  by this  emotionally although they're definitely  not crying or anything it's just like  rain on their face okay guys it's just  rain ochako seems to be especially moved  by this situation as we might have  expected  but she doesn't approach deku again she  decides to give him his space for now  and then the class